          '\n'
          'that day.\n'
          '\n'
          '13\n'
          '\n'
          '2.14 Paragraphs 3.3 to 3.8 in Part (3) of the Guidelines set out '
          'the points to note as regards\n'
          '\n'
          'interaction with other customers’ dogs.\n'
          '\n'
          '2.15 Where necessary, dog strollers (if any) should be folded up or '
          'put away to make way',
  'type': 'CompositeElement'},
 {'element_id': '70866bcd-c521-47a4-9d1d-0050901f7e4b',
  'metadata': {'file_directory': './KnowledgeFiles',
               'filename': 'Guidelines on Good Practices and Behaviour for '
                           'Dog-Friendly Restaurants.pdf',
               'filetype': 'application/pdf',
               'languages': ['eng'],
               'last_modified': '2026-10-10T22:34:42',
               'orig_elements': '',
               'page_number': 14},
  'text': 'for others.\n'
          '\n'
          'Maintaining a clean environment in restaurants\n'
          '\n'
          '2.16 In case of fouling of the restaurant by dog excrement, the '
          'relevant customer should take\n'
          '\n'
          'the responsibility to promptly clean up and properly dispose of the '
          'excrement (e.g. by\n'
          '\n'
          'wrapping the excrement in a sealed bag for proper disposal in '
          'dog-specific trash bins),\n'
          '\n'
          'and notify the restaurant staff to inspect the area or carry out '
          'further disinfection, so as to',
  'type': 'CompositeElement'},
 {'element_id': 'd45adda4-c51d-452a-9f0a-a21552b708b5',
  'metadata': {'file_directory': './KnowledgeFiles',
               'filename': 'Guidelines on Good Practices and Behaviour for '
                           'Dog-Friendly Restaurants.pdf',
               'filetype': 'application/pdf',
               'languages': ['eng'],
               'last_modified': '2026-10-10T22:34:42',
               'orig_elements': '',
               'page_number': 14},
  'text': 'maintain good environmental hygiene. After the clean-up, the '
          'customer should\n'
          '\n'
          'thoroughly wash and disinfect his hands.\n'
          '\n'
          '2.17 If the customer bringing the dog refuses to clean up, fails to '
          'complete the clean-up within\n'
          '\n'
          'a reasonable timeframe, or fails to restore the restaurant to its '
          'basic hygienic condition,\n'
          '\n'
          'the restaurant has the right to undertake the cleaning by its own '
          'staff and may therefore\n'
          '\n'
          'charge a cleaning fee. In general, restaurants will specify, in '
          'their “Notes to Customers”',
  'type': 'CompositeElement'},
 {'element_id': '2d4e4926-d7a7-40a2-90bc-66e4ab4fc9ac',
  'metadata': {'file_directory': './KnowledgeFiles',
               'filename': 'Guidelines on Good Practices and Behaviour for '
