 {'element_id': '3b3b6b30-58a4-4c1b-aae4-68ccdc6aa7e2',
  'metadata': {'file_directory': './KnowledgeFiles',
               'filename': 'Guidelines on Good Practices and Behaviour for '
                           'Dog-Friendly Restaurants.pdf',
               'filetype': 'application/pdf',
               'languages': ['eng'],
               'last_modified': '2026-10-10T22:34:42',
               'orig_elements': '',
               'page_number': 14},
  'text': 'Response to incidents\n'
          '\n'
          '2.19 In the event that a dog bites a customer or staff, the '
          'customer bringing the dog should\n'
          '\n'
          'handle the matter in accordance with the Rabies Ordinance (Cap. '
          '421), which includes\n'
          '\n'
          'reporting the incident to the Police immediately, detaining the dog '
          'securely in isolation\n'
          '\n'
          'from other animals, and facilitating the follow-up procedures. '
          'Non-compliance may\n'
          '\n'
          'result in prosecution.\n'
          '\n'
          '2.20 If other dog-related disputes or incidents arise on the '
          'premises, the customer bringing the',
  'type': 'CompositeElement'},
 {'element_id': '7e2b0f35-d283-4d16-bddb-7869ef2a559d',
  'metadata': {'file_directory': './KnowledgeFiles',
               'filename': 'Guidelines on Good Practices and Behaviour for '
                           'Dog-Friendly Restaurants.pdf',
               'filetype': 'application/pdf',
               'languages': ['eng'],
               'last_modified': '2026-10-10T22:34:42',
               'orig_elements': '',
               'page_number': 14},
  'text': 'dog should keep calm, follow the advice of the restaurant staff and '
          'negotiate with other\n'
          '\n'
          'customers to resolve the matter.\n'
          '\n'
          '14\n'
          '\n'
          '(3) Guidelines on Good Behaviour for Customers Without Dogs',
  'type': 'CompositeElement'},
 {'element_id': 'fb6743d2-45ac-4bc8-94c6-c7f6b132e4d7',
  'metadata': {'file_directory': './KnowledgeFiles',
               'filename': 'Guidelines on Good Practices and Behaviour for '
                           'Dog-Friendly Restaurants.pdf',
               'filetype': 'application/pdf',
               'languages': ['eng'],
               'last_modified': '2026-10-10T22:34:42',
               'orig_elements': '',
               'page_number': 15},
  'text': 'Introduction\n'
          '\n'
          '3.1\n'
          '\n'
          'The Food Business Regulation (Cap. 132X) has been amended to allow '
          'dogs to enter\n'
          '\n'
          'permitted food premises (i.e. permitted restaurants) under '
          'specified circumstances.\n'
          '\n'
          'Any person engaged in a food business and persons bringing dogs '
          'must comply with\n'
          '\n'
          'the statutory requirements. Restaurant licensees must also comply '
          'with the licensing\n'
          '\n'
          'conditions. The third part of the Guidelines sets out the good '
          'practices for reference',
  'type': 'CompositeElement'},
 {'element_id': '61f57767-874a-4717-8052-19e15089fd0f',
  'metadata': {'file_directory': './KnowledgeFiles',
               'filename': 'Guidelines on Good Practices and Behaviour for '
                           'Dog-Friendly Restaurants.pdf',
               'filetype': 'application/pdf',
               'languages': ['eng'],
               'last_modified': '2026-10-10T22:34:42',
               'orig_elements': '',
               'page_number': 15},
  'text': 'of customers without dogs when interacting with dogs in permitted '
          'restaurants, with the\n'
          '\n'
          'aim of promoting mutual respect and harmony with pets.\n'
          '\n'
          'Before entering a restaurant\n'
          '\n'
          '3.2\n'
          '\n'
          'Permitted restaurants are required to display, at all times and at '
          'a conspicuous place at\n'
          '\n'
          'the entrance, designated signages (see Annex 1) so that the public '
          'can make an informed\n'
          '\n'
          'choice. People who patronise the permitted restaurants should be '
          'aware that dogs may',
  'type': 'CompositeElement'},
 {'element_id': '2c08ec85-7384-438b-a724-fc138c8f80d4',
  'metadata': {'file_directory': './KnowledgeFiles',
               'filename': 'Guidelines on Good Practices and Behaviour for '
                           'Dog-Friendly Restaurants.pdf',
               'filetype': 'application/pdf',
               'languages': ['eng'],
               'last_modified': '2026-10-10T22:34:42',
               'orig_elements': '',
               'page_number': 15},
  'text': 'be present. Mutual respect and tolerance are important to help '
          'maintain a comfortable\n'
          '\n'
          'and harmonious dining environment for everyone.',
  'type': 'CompositeElement'},
 {'element_id': '6b22e26c-c687-4a6f-9ed6-f7c3c97b3e4a',
  'metadata': {'file_directory': './KnowledgeFiles',
               'filename': 'Guidelines on Good Practices and Behaviour for '
                           'Dog-Friendly Restaurants.pdf',
               'filetype': 'application/pdf',
               'languages': ['eng'],
               'last_modified': '2026-10-10T22:34:42',
               'orig_elements': '',
               'page_number': 15},
  'text': 'Interactions with dogs\n'
          '\n'
          '3.3 Obtain the consent from the dog owner before touching, petting '
          'or photographing a dog.\n'
          '\n'
          '3.4 Do not feed other customers’ dogs.\n'
          '\n'
          '3.5 Avoid actions that may disturb or frighten the dogs, such as '
          'making sudden loud noises\n'
          '\n'
          'or playfully tempting them with food, so as to reduce the risk of '
          'accidents.\n'
          '\n'
          '3.6 Do not attempt to leash, push or shoo away other customers’ '
          'dogs, so as to prevent',
  'type': 'CompositeElement'},
 {'element_id': '9c28dd58-d488-4d0b-b3c4-8daaa08b0472',
  'metadata': {'file_directory': './KnowledgeFiles',
               'filename': 'Guidelines on Good Practices and Behaviour for '
                           'Dog-Friendly Restaurants.pdf',
               'filetype': 'application/pdf',
               'languages': ['eng'],
               'last_modified': '2026-10-10T22:34:42',
               'orig_elements': '',
               'page_number': 15},
  'text': 'misunderstandings or safety risks.\n'
          '\n'
          '3.7\n'
          '\n'
          'If a dog’s behaviour is causing disturbance or inconvenience, '
          'report it to the restaurant\n'
          '\n'
          'staff first so that they can take appropriate actions.\n'
          '\n'
          '3.8\n'
          '\n'
          'Store personal belongings and handbags properly to prevent damage '
          'from dogs.\n'
          '\n'
          '15\n'
          '\n'
          '3.9\n'
          '\n'
          'If unfortunately bitten by a dog, remain calm and seek assistance '
          'from restaurant staff.\n'
          '\n'
          'According to the statutory requirements, the dog owner shall report '
          'the incident to the',
  'type': 'CompositeElement'},
 {'element_id': '589ffdf8-8f67-4791-9064-d2958f3f35e2',
  'metadata': {'file_directory': './KnowledgeFiles',
               'filename': 'Guidelines on Good Practices and Behaviour for '
                           'Dog-Friendly Restaurants.pdf',
               'filetype': 'application/pdf',
               'languages': ['eng'],
               'last_modified': '2026-10-10T22:34:42',
               'orig_elements': '',
               'page_number': 16},
  'text': 'Police. If necessary, the injured person may also call the Police '
          'on his own.\n'
          '\n'
          '16\n'
          '\n'
          '17\n'
          '\n'
          '18\n'
          '\n'
          '19',
  'type': 'CompositeElement'}]
