2026-10-11 16:00:04 - __main__ - INFO - Document content: [{'element_id': 'b95d38a3-f485-4242-80b6-91f2bb8f0407',
  'metadata': {'file_directory': './KnowledgeFiles',
               'filename': 'code_of_practice.pdf',
               'filetype': 'application/pdf',
               'languages': ['eng'],
               'last_modified': '2026-10-10T22:37:47',
               'orig_elements': '',
               'page_number': 1},
  'text': '實務守則\n'
          '\n'
          '處所獲批讓狗隻處於食物業處所的准許：店主／員工應如何即場處理事故\n'
          '\n'
          '本指引適用於獲食物環境衞生署（食環署）批准容許狗隻進入的食肆，供持牌人、店主、經理及前線員工於沒有政府人員在場時，如何先行／即場處理狗吠、撲人、失 '
          '控、衞生問題及狗主不合作等事故之用。\n'
          '\n'
          '基本原則\n'
          '\n'
          '持牌人須確保處所運作符合食環署牌照條件、食物安全要求及良好作業安排；員工亦應知悉，若發現違規或危險行為，應如何即時應對及向其上級匯報。\n'
          '\n'
          '如有即時危險、有人受傷、狗隻追逐或咬人事故，應先保障現場人士安全，並立即報警處理；如狗隻仍未受控，警方會即時轉交漁農自然護理署到現場 '
          '跟進；如狗隻已受控，漁農自然護理署在收到警方轉介後，聯絡狗主跟進。如狗主或店方涉及違反食物業規例或牌照條件，食環署接報後會作出跟進(市 '
          '民可致電1823提出建議、詢問及投訴)。\n'
          '\n'
          '即場處理步驟\n'
          '\n'
          '判斷風險\n'
          '\n'
          '第一步\n'
          '\n'
          '先迅速判斷事件屬於以下那種類別：一般狗吠、持續滋擾、撲人／追逐、咬人、排泄／污染、或狗主拒絕配合。\n'
          '\n'
          '如見到狗隻已有衝前、露齒、撲向他人、追逐、打鬥或咬傷跡象，應視為高風險情況，不應只作一般勸喻。\n'
          '\n'
          '即時口頭指示\n'
          '\n'
          '第二步',
  'type': 'CompositeElement'},
 {'element_id': '02cca2aa-1738-48e4-852d-09c175fa1866',
  'metadata': {'file_directory': './KnowledgeFiles',
               'filename': 'code_of_practice.pdf',
               'filetype': 'application/pdf',
               'languages': ['eng'],
               'last_modified': '2026-10-10T22:37:47',
               'orig_elements': '',
               'page_number': 1},
  'text': '店主或員工應立即以清晰而簡短方式要求狗主控制狗隻，例如要求縮短狗帶、將狗隻帶回座位旁、停止接近其他客人， 或立即把狗隻帶離處所範圍。\n'
          '\n'
          '如餐廳守則已列明相關要求，應直接按守則執行，避免與狗主爭論法理細節。\n'
          '\n'
          '分隔人群及保護現場人士\n'
          '\n'
          '第三步\n'
          '\n'
          '如情況有升級風險／跡象，應先安排受影響客人離開相關區域，避免客人圍觀、挑釁或觸碰狗隻，並暫停安排客人坐 近涉事位置。\n'
          '\n'
          '如有食物、器皿或熱飲接近涉事位置，應盡快移走，以減低人身及食物安全風險。\n'
          '\n'
          '按情況採取措施\n'
          '\n'
          '第四步\n'
          '\n'
          '如屬一般滋擾而狗主採取合作態度，可要求即時改善，例如安撫狗隻、減少刺激、帶狗到較少人的位置，或短暫帶同 '
          '狗隻離開處所，待冷靜後再決定是否重返。\n'
          '\n'
          '如狗隻持續失控、撲人、追逐、造成恐慌或有機會影響其他客人安全，持牌人／店主／經理／員工應要求狗主帶同狗 '
          '隻立即離場；如拒絕合作或有即時危險，應立即報警處理。\n'
          '\n'
          '記錄及上報\n'
          '\n'
          '第五步\n'
          '\n'
          '員工應記錄涉事時間、桌號／位置、狗隻特徵、相關人士資料、店鋪採取的措施、是否有人受傷、是否有閉路電視片 '
          '段／錄影紀錄，並向店長或持牌人匯報。',
  'type': 'CompositeElement'},
 {'element_id': '4d042221-d8a6-4c8b-9db1-40e6e65fcccc',
  'metadata': {'file_directory': './KnowledgeFiles',
               'filename': 'code_of_practice.pdf',
               'filetype': 'application/pdf',
               'languages': ['eng'],
               'last_modified': '2026-10-10T22:37:47',
               'orig_elements': '',
               'page_number': 1},
  'text': '如事件涉及咬人(根據法例第421章<<狂犬病條例>>狗隻蓄養人須將該事實通知最近的警署，不得延誤）、格鬥狗隻或 '
          '已知危險狗隻、狗隻嚴重失控、或涉嫌違反食環署牌照條件，必須向警方、漁護署及食環署作後續通報。\n'
          '\n'
          '持牌人可做及應做的事項\n'
          '\n'
          '持牌人可制定及執行處所守則，包括要求狗隻必須由成年人牽引、限制狗隻進入範圍、拒絕不受控制的狗隻進入，以及要求違規／不配合的狗主帶同狗 '
          '隻離場。\n'
          '\n'
          '持牌人應培訓員工、張貼標示、確保現場衞生狀況妥當、設有處理突發事故的程序，並在有需要時作出即時干預，而不應採取放任態度讓情況惡化。\n'
          '\n'
          '當處理不足時\n'
          '\n'
          '若店方明知狗隻持續失控、撲人、追逐、咬人、排泄或違反處所守則，惟沒有作出勸止、要求狗主配合、要求狗主帶同狗隻離場，甚至發現有即時危險 '
          '時卻沒有上報相關政府部門，會可能被視為管理不足，不符合良好作業要求，或已違反牌照或准許條件的風險。',
  'type': 'CompositeElement'},
 {'element_id': 'eea0c5fc-15e5-4314-b0c5-ce08d95512ce',
  'metadata': {'file_directory': './KnowledgeFiles',
               'filename': 'code_of_practice.pdf',
               'filetype': 'application/pdf',
               'languages': ['eng'],
               'last_modified': '2026-10-10T22:37:47',
               'orig_elements': '',
               'page_number': 1},
  'text': '正如上述，若情況已構成即時危險，但店方仍採取愛理不理態度，除了涉嫌違反牌照或准許條件外，亦可能增加民事責任及在場人士受傷的風險。\n'
          '\n'
          '為保障大眾安全與店內秩序，請各位寵物飼主務必配合立即縮短狗帶並控制狗隻； '
          '如未能即時控制，本店將會請你帶同狗隻離開，亦可能向相關政府部門舉報此事件。\n'
          '\n'
          'Code of Practice',
  'type': 'CompositeElement'},
 {'element_id': 'f508495c-87ce-49c2-bf36-7f49124957b1',
  'metadata': {'file_directory': './KnowledgeFiles',
               'filename': 'code_of_practice.pdf',
               'filetype': 'application/pdf',
               'languages': ['eng'],
               'last_modified': '2026-10-10T22:37:47',
               'orig_elements': '',
               'page_number': 2},
  'text': 'Food Premises Permitted to Admit Dogs: On-site Management by '
          'Restaurant Owners/Staff\n'
          '\n'
          'This Guideline is applicable to local food premises permitted by '
          'the Food and Environmental Hygiene Department (FEHD) to admit dogs, '
          'and is for reference of licensees, restaurant owners, managers, and '
          'frontline staff in handling situations such as dogs’ barking, '
          'lunging at people, loss of control, hygiene issues, and '
          'uncooperative dog owners in the absence of government officers.',
  'type': 'CompositeElement'},
 {'element_id': 'f7a451d4-a5a0-4475-8ef1-818e1825dd5e',
  'metadata': {'file_directory': './KnowledgeFiles',
               'filename': 'code_of_practice.pdf',
               'filetype': 'application/pdf',
               'languages': ['eng'],
               'last_modified': '2026-10-10T22:37:47',
               'orig_elements': '',
               'page_number': 2},
  'text': 'Basic Principles\n'
          '\n'
          'Licensees must ensure that their premises are operated in '
          'accordance with the licensing conditions of the FEHD, the relevant '
          'food safety requirements and the Guidelines on Good Practices and '
          'Behaviour. If any non-compliance or dangerous behaviour is '
          'observed, staff should know how to deal with it immediately and '
          'report it to their supervisors.',
  'type': 'CompositeElement'},
 {'element_id': '53eaf698-3ed9-4f9c-8967-64b98c029af9',
  'metadata': {'file_directory': './KnowledgeFiles',
               'filename': 'code_of_practice.pdf',
               'filetype': 'application/pdf',
               'languages': ['eng'],
               'last_modified': '2026-10-10T22:37:47',
               'orig_elements': '',
               'page_number': 2},
  'text': 'In the event of any imminent danger, injuries, dogs’ chasing or '
          'biting people, ensure the safety of everyone on the premises first '
          'and call the Police immediately. If the dog remains uncontrolled, '
          'the Police will immediately refer the case to the Agriculture, '
          'Fisheries and Conservation Department (AFCD) for on-site follow-up. '
          'If the dog is already under control, AFCD will contact the dog '
          'owner for follow-up upon receiving the referral from the Police. '
          'Should the dog owner or the restaurant',
  'type': 'CompositeElement'},
 {'element_id': 'f606c3d5-42fc-4f9b-92ed-040e3992124b',
  'metadata': {'file_directory': './KnowledgeFiles',
               'filename': 'code_of_practice.pdf',
               'filetype': 'application/pdf',
               'is_continuation': True,
               'languages': ['eng'],
               'last_modified': '2026-10-10T22:37:47',
               'orig_elements': '',
               'page_number': 2},
  'text': 'operator be found to have violated food business regulations or '
          'licensing conditions, the FEHD will take follow-up action upon '
          'receipt of the report. (Members of the public may call 1823 to make '
          'suggestions, enquiries, or complaints.)',
  'type': 'CompositeElement'},
 {'element_id': 'b3650b9b-2869-4b8d-9560-48ba357b7fab',
  'metadata': {'file_directory': './KnowledgeFiles',
               'filename': 'code_of_practice.pdf',
               'filetype': 'application/pdf',
               'languages': ['eng'],
               'last_modified': '2026-10-10T22:37:47',
               'orig_elements': '',
               'page_number': 2},
  'text': 'Steps for On-Site Handling of an Incident\n\nAssessing risks',
  'type': 'CompositeElement'},
 {'element_id': '73695a29-38f5-4386-b14e-ecf0bb8c16db',
  'metadata': {'file_directory': './KnowledgeFiles',
               'filename': 'code_of_practice.pdf',
               'filetype': 'application/pdf',
               'languages': ['eng'],
               'last_modified': '2026-10-10T22:37:47',
               'orig_elements': '',
               'page_number': 2},
  'text': 'Step 1\n'
          '\n'
          'First, promptly determine which of the following categories the '
          'incident falls into: normal barking, persistent nuisance, lunging '
          'at people/chasing, biting people, defecation/soiling, or dog '
          'owners’ refusal to cooperate.\n'
          '\n'
          'If a dog shows signs of rushing forward, baring teeth, lunging at '
          'people, chasing, fighting or biting, it should be regarded as a '
          'high-risk situation and should not be handled by way of mere '
          'general advice.\n'
          '\n'
          'Issue verbal instructions immediately',
  'type': 'CompositeElement'},
 {'element_id': '86cdbeb4-fe3b-42c9-aed0-2fd504d1d8a1',
  'metadata': {'file_directory': './KnowledgeFiles',
               'filename': 'code_of_practice.pdf',
               'filetype': 'application/pdf',
               'languages': ['eng'],
               'last_modified': '2026-10-10T22:37:47',
               'orig_elements': '',
               'page_number': 2},
  'text': 'Step 2\n'
          '\n'
          'The restaurant owner or staff should immediately require, in a '
          'clear and concise manner, the dog owner to control the dog by, for '
          'examples, shortening the dog leashes, bringing the dog back to his '
          'seat, stopping the dog from approaching other customers or removing '
          'the dog from the indoor area immediately.\n'
          '\n'
          'If the relevant requirements are already stated in the house rules, '
          'enforce them directly, and avoid getting into arguments with the '
          'dog owners over legal details.',
  'type': 'CompositeElement'},
 {'element_id': 'dab11fa6-61fd-41ee-ba3d-f6fd9ff55a3e',
  'metadata': {'file_directory': './KnowledgeFiles',
               'filename': 'code_of_practice.pdf',
               'filetype': 'application/pdf',
               'languages': ['eng'],
               'last_modified': '2026-10-10T22:37:47',
               'orig_elements': '',
               'page_number': 2},
  'text': 'Separate the crowd and ensure the safety of the scene\n'
          '\n'
          'Step 3\n'
          '\n'
          'If the situation is escalating, arrange for the affected customers '
          'to leave the scene first, prevent other customers from gathering '
          'around, provoking, or touching the dog, and suspend seating new '
          'customers near the incident location.\n'
          '\n'
          'Any food, utensils or hot drinks near the incident location should '
          'be removed as soon as possible to reduce risks to people and food '
          'safety.\n'
          '\n'
          'Take measures as appropriate',
  'type': 'CompositeElement'},
 {'element_id': '35fef112-2ba0-4006-811a-acc52b6fa752',
  'metadata': {'file_directory': './KnowledgeFiles',
               'filename': 'code_of_practice.pdf',
               'filetype': 'application/pdf',
               'languages': ['eng'],
               'last_modified': '2026-10-10T22:37:47',
               'orig_elements': '',
               'page_number': 2},
  'text': 'Step 4\n'
          '\n'
          'For a general disturbance where the dog owner is cooperative, '
          'request the owner to make prompt improvements, for examples, to '
          'calm the dog, reduce stimuli, take the dog to a location with fewer '
          'people, or temporarily remove the dog from the premises and decide '
          'whether to return after calming it down.',
  'type': 'CompositeElement'},
 {'element_id': '987c3660-4b2d-45fb-963d-bddb84a645a1',
  'metadata': {'file_directory': './KnowledgeFiles',
               'filename': 'code_of_practice.pdf',
               'filetype': 'application/pdf',
               'languages': ['eng'],
               'last_modified': '2026-10-10T22:37:47',
               'orig_elements': '',
               'page_number': 2},
  'text': 'If a dog is persistently out of control, or if it lunges at people, '
          'chases around, creates a panic or poses a safety risk to other '
          'customers, the licensee should ask the dog owner to immediately '
          'leave the premises with the dog. In the case of non-cooperation or '
          'imminent danger, call the Police immediately.\n'
          '\n'
          'Record and report',
  'type': 'CompositeElement'},
 {'element_id': '28e6a17f-530a-4107-886e-0623b8bc262b',
  'metadata': {'file_directory': './KnowledgeFiles',
               'filename': 'code_of_practice.pdf',
               'filetype': 'application/pdf',
               'languages': ['eng'],
               'last_modified': '2026-10-10T22:37:47',
               'orig_elements': '',
               'page_number': 2},
  'text': 'Step 5\n'
          '\n'
          'Record and report to the shop manager or the licensee the time of '
          'the incident, the table number/location, distinguishing features of '
          'the dog involved, details of the individuals involved, measures '
          'taken by staff, whether anyone was injured, and whether CCTV '
          'footage is available.',
  'type': 'CompositeElement'},
 {'element_id': '9816394d-800c-4b53-9c19-062d46c14d26',
  'metadata': {'file_directory': './KnowledgeFiles',
               'filename': 'code_of_practice.pdf',
               'filetype': 'application/pdf',
               'languages': ['eng'],
               'last_modified': '2026-10-10T22:37:47',
               'orig_elements': '',
               'page_number': 2},
  'text': 'If the incident involves a bite (Under the Rabies Ordinance (Cap. '
          '421), its keeper must immediately report the incident to the '
          'nearest police station without delay), fighting dog or a known '
          'dangerous dog, severe loss of control, or a possible breach of the '
          'FEHD’s licensing conditions, consideration should be given to '
          'making a follow-up report to the Police, the AFCD or the FEHD.\n'
          '\n'
          'In the Event of Inadequate Management',
  'type': 'CompositeElement'},
 {'element_id': 'c643b070-84cf-434d-8349-cba003c8b986',
  'metadata': {'file_directory': './KnowledgeFiles',
               'filename': 'code_of_practice.pdf',
               'filetype': 'application/pdf',
               'languages': ['eng'],
               'last_modified': '2026-10-10T22:37:47',
               'orig_elements': '',
               'page_number': 2},
  'text': 'If a restaurant operator is aware that a dog is persistently out of '
          'control, lunging at people, chasing, biting, defecating, or '
          'violating the house rules but fails to intervene, request the '
          'owner’s cooperation, consider asking the owner to leave, or report '
          'the case to the concerned government department or the restaurant '
          'management when necessary, this may be regarded as inadequate '
          'management that fails to meet the requirements on good practice. It '
          'may also pose risks regarding the conditions of',
  'type': 'CompositeElement'},
 {'element_id': '42167613-bcb6-4525-b942-9c90a9319794',
  'metadata': {'file_directory': './KnowledgeFiles',
               'filename': 'code_of_practice.pdf',
               'filetype': 'application/pdf',
               'is_continuation': True,
               'languages': ['eng'],
               'last_modified': '2026-10-10T22:37:47',
               'orig_elements': '',
               'page_number': 2},
  'text': 'the license or permission.',
  'type': 'CompositeElement'},
 {'element_id': '0683aa8a-7dd3-4e53-aee3-97490a5a1a86',
  'metadata': {'file_directory': './KnowledgeFiles',
               'filename': 'code_of_practice.pdf',
               'filetype': 'application/pdf',
               'languages': ['eng'],
               'last_modified': '2026-10-10T22:37:47',
               'orig_elements': '',
               'page_number': 2},
  'text': 'If a situation poses an immediate danger but the restaurant '
          'operator still adopts an indifferent attitude, this may not only '
          'pose licensing risks but also increase the risks of civil liability '
          'and on-site injuries.',
  'type': 'CompositeElement'},
 {'element_id': '1c0b37ce-f467-494e-8b60-894b09ef84cd',
  'metadata': {'file_directory': './KnowledgeFiles',
               'filename': 'code_of_practice.pdf',
               'filetype': 'application/pdf',
               'languages': ['eng'],
               'last_modified': '2026-10-10T22:37:47',
               'orig_elements': '',
               'page_number': 2},
  'text': 'To ensure public safety and maintain order in the restaurant, all '
          'pet owners must cooperate by shortening promptly the leashes of '
          'their dogs and keeping their dogs under control. If you are unable '
          'to control your dog, please remove your dog from the restaurant; '
          'otherwise, we will report the incident to the relevant government '
          'departments.',
  'type': 'CompositeElement'}]
2026-10-11 16:00:05 - unstructured - WARNING - No languages specified, defaulting to English.
2026-10-11 16:00:05 - __main__ - INFO - Document content: [{'element_id': '95d4818f-4138-4203-a666-ce0acea71abf',
  'metadata': {'file_directory': './KnowledgeFiles',
               'filename': 'Licensing_conditions.pdf',
               'filetype': 'application/pdf',
               'languages': ['eng'],
               'last_modified': '2026-10-10T22:33:54',
               'orig_elements': '',
               'page_number': 1},
  'text': 'Licensing Conditions for Permission for Presence of Dogs on Food '
          'Premises',
  'type': 'CompositeElement'},
 {'element_id': 'a9182b21-aa7b-471f-91b8-ba0fc9b8716b',
  'metadata': {'file_directory': './KnowledgeFiles',
               'filename': 'Licensing_conditions.pdf',
               'filetype': 'application/pdf',
               'languages': ['eng'],
               'last_modified': '2026-10-10T22:33:54',
               'orig_elements': '',
               'page_number': 1},
  'text': '1. An A3 size signage designated by the Food and Environmental '
          'Hygiene Department shall be displayed at all times and at a '
          'conspicuous place near the main entrances for the customers of the '
          'premises, indicating that presence of dogs is permitted on the '
          'premises. The signage must be clearly visible to customers from '
          'outside of the premises, and must not be obstructed by any object. '
          'The licensee shall comply with instructions given by the Director '
          'of Food and Environmental Hygiene regarding the',
  'type': 'CompositeElement'},
 {'element_id': '4999b163-998e-4fc0-93f4-a3f35e774524',
  'metadata': {'file_directory': './KnowledgeFiles',
               'filename': 'Licensing_conditions.pdf',
               'filetype': 'application/pdf',
               'is_continuation': True,
               'languages': ['eng'],
               'last_modified': '2026-10-10T22:33:54',
               'orig_elements': '',
               'page_number': 1},
  'text': 'way the signage is displayed.',
  'type': 'CompositeElement'},
 {'element_id': 'f9b15606-55f3-4260-955a-5525608ccbb9',
  'metadata': {'file_directory': './KnowledgeFiles',
               'filename': 'Licensing_conditions.pdf',
               'filetype': 'application/pdf',
               'languages': ['eng'],
               'last_modified': '2026-10-10T22:33:54',
               'orig_elements': '',
               'page_number': 1},
  'text': '2. No cooking or preparation of dog food on the premises is '
          'allowed.\n'
          '\n'
          '3. Only prepackaged dry dog food, vacuum-packed dog food and canned '
          'dog food can be sold or provided on the premises.\n'
          '\n'
          '4. Cooking or heating of food on dining table (including open flame '
          'or using electric heating apparatus, except for candles and '
          'electric coasters for keeping beverages warm) are not allowed at '
          'any time.\n'
          '\n'
          '5. No dog shall be allowed on any dining table at any time.',
  'type': 'CompositeElement'},
 {'element_id': '76691cf0-d72a-41c5-9dca-63f90d801218',
  'metadata': {'file_directory': './KnowledgeFiles',
               'filename': 'Licensing_conditions.pdf',
               'filetype': 'application/pdf',
               'languages': ['eng'],
               'last_modified': '2026-10-10T22:33:54',
               'orig_elements': '',
               'page_number': 1},
  'text': '6. Reusable utensils shall not be provided to dog by the premises. '
          'Only single-use non-plastic eating utensils or crockery may be sold '
          'or provided to dog owners for use by dogs.\n'
          '\n'
          '7. All poisonous baits or pest/rodent-trapping devices on the '
          'premises shall be kept out of reach of dogs.\n'
          '\n'
          '8.\n'
          '\n'
          'In case of fouling of the premises by dog excrement, the affected '
          'area must be thoroughly cleansed and disinfected immediately to '
          'maintain the hygienic condition of the premises.',
  'type': 'CompositeElement'},
 {'element_id': '11c9c252-e339-4d3d-9652-f482d143b92c',
  'metadata': {'file_directory': './KnowledgeFiles',
               'filename': 'Licensing_conditions.pdf',
               'filetype': 'application/pdf',
               'languages': ['eng'],
               'last_modified': '2026-10-10T22:33:54',
               'orig_elements': '',
               'page_number': 1},
  'text': '9. No customer with dog shall be allowed to sit on the bar counter '
          'seats unless the food counter or food preparation area is '
          'segregated from the seating accommodation by a permanently fixed '
          'partition carried to the full height of the premises.\n'
          '\n'
          '10. No dog shall be allowed to enter the zone within 1.5 m of any '
          'buffet counter / salad bar.',
  'type': 'CompositeElement'},
 {'element_id': '4d2b1120-22b7-4e94-9216-2bb2264a1bd0',
  'metadata': {'file_directory': './KnowledgeFiles',
               'filename': 'Licensing_conditions.pdf',
               'filetype': 'application/pdf',
               'languages': ['eng'],
               'last_modified': '2026-10-10T22:33:54',
               'orig_elements': '',
               'page_number': 1},
  'text': '11. Where a dog causes injury to any person on the premises and the '
          'incident is reported to the Police, the licensee shall report the '
          'same incident to the Director of Food and Environmental Hygiene by '
          'using the attached prescribed form within 2 working days from the '
          'date of the incident.',
  'type': 'CompositeElement'}]
2026-10-11 16:00:05 - unstructured - WARNING - No languages specified, defaulting to English.
2026-10-11 16:00:05 - __main__ - INFO - Document content: [{'element_id': 'c88a856d-dc88-4a90-9ff6-7b1fa6386677',
  'metadata': {'file_directory': './KnowledgeFiles',
               'filename': 'faq.pdf',
               'filetype': 'application/pdf',
               'languages': ['eng'],
               'last_modified': '2026-10-10T22:36:54',
               'orig_elements': '',
               'page_number': 1},
  'text': 'Permission for Presence of Dogs on Food Premises\n'
          '\n'
          'Frequently Asked Questions\n'
          '\n'
          'Statutory Requirements\n'
          '\n'
          'Q1: What are the specific responsibilities of the operator if the '
          'application is successful?\n'
          '\n'
          'A1: Approved restaurant operators must comply with relevant '
          'legislation and licensing\n'
          '\n'
          'conditions to safeguard the safety of both humans and animals, as '
          'well as to ensure food',
  'type': 'CompositeElement'},
 {'element_id': '40ff1e57-4e3c-4e82-b4f1-24d9c37a0fc5',
  'metadata': {'file_directory': './KnowledgeFiles',
               'filename': 'faq.pdf',
               'filetype': 'application/pdf',
               'languages': ['eng'],
               'last_modified': '2026-10-10T22:36:54',
               'orig_elements': '',
               'page_number': 1},
  'text': 'safety and environmental hygiene.\n'
          '\n'
          'Regarding legal requirements, restaurant operators must ensure that '
          'all statutory\n'
          '\n'
          'requirements are met before allowing customers to bring dogs onto '
          'the premises, including:\n'
          '\n'
          '(a) The restaurant has obtained permission to admit dogs;\n'
          '\n'
          '(b) The dog entering the food premises is not a “fighting dog” or a '
          '“known dangerous dog”;\n'
          '\n'
          '(c) At all times when the dog is present on the food premises, the '
          'dog is on a leash of not',
  'type': 'CompositeElement'},
 {'element_id': '3a187fd2-217d-479d-a198-26a88cf4e681',
  'metadata': {'file_directory': './KnowledgeFiles',
               'filename': 'faq.pdf',
               'filetype': 'application/pdf',
               'languages': ['eng'],
               'last_modified': '2026-10-10T22:36:54',
               'orig_elements': '',
               'page_number': 1},
  'text': 'more than 1.5 metres in length either securely held by an adult or '
          'securely tied to a',
  'type': 'CompositeElement'},
 {'element_id': '78baafc1-24be-45d1-be2c-2c0e50a98b7a',
  'metadata': {'file_directory': './KnowledgeFiles',
               'filename': 'faq.pdf',
               'filetype': 'application/pdf',
               'languages': ['eng'],
               'last_modified': '2026-10-10T22:36:54',
               'orig_elements': '',
               'page_number': 1},
  'text': 'fixture; and\n'
          '\n'
          '(d) The dog is not present in a food room when it is present on the '
          'food premises.\n'
          '\n'
          'Furthermore, restaurant operators are required to observe various '
          'licensing conditions to\n'
          '\n'
          'maintain hygiene and safety standards. The Food and Environmental '
          'Hygiene Department\n'
          '\n'
          '(FEHD) will prepare a set of "Guideline on Good Practices and '
          'Behaviour" for reference,\n'
          '\n'
          'which will provide advice on matters within the discretion of '
          'restaurant operators and',
  'type': 'CompositeElement'},
 {'element_id': '9c70a73b-8fae-46c7-855a-50d99047a7fa',
  'metadata': {'file_directory': './KnowledgeFiles',
               'filename': 'faq.pdf',
               'filetype': 'application/pdf',
               'languages': ['eng'],
               'last_modified': '2026-10-10T22:36:54',
               'orig_elements': '',
               'page_number': 1},
  'text': 'factors that they may wish to take into account when exercising '
          'such discretion.\n'
          '\n'
          'Q2: The legislation requires that dogs must be leashed when '
          'entering a restaurant. What\n'
          '\n'
          'other details should be noted?\n'
          '\n'
          'A2: According to statutory requirements, dogs must be on a leash of '
          'not more than 1.5 meters\n'
          '\n'
          'in length either securely held by an adult or securely tied to a '
          'fixture.\n'
          '\n'
          'This requirement is to ensure that the dog remains under proper '
          'control while on the',
  'type': 'CompositeElement'},
 {'element_id': 'eaf9aa53-0805-430f-82e2-3644fcf1ce9f',
  'metadata': {'file_directory': './KnowledgeFiles',
               'filename': 'faq.pdf',
               'filetype': 'application/pdf',
               'languages': ['eng'],
               'last_modified': '2026-10-10T22:36:54',
               'orig_elements': '',
               'page_number': 2},
  'text': 'premises. Therefore, before allowing a customer with a dog to '
          'enter, restaurant staff should\n'
          '\n'
          'check whether the customer is an adult and whether the length of '
          'the leash complies with\n'
          '\n'
          'the legal requirement, among other things. If in doubt, staff '
          'should communicate clearly\n'
          '\n'
          'with the customer before entry to avoid any contravention.\n'
          '\n'
          'Furthermore, if a customer wishes to securely tie the dog to a '
          'fixed structure, that structure',
  'type': 'CompositeElement'},
 {'element_id': '97df3fd0-eda7-4371-90a1-75a0af8e5dac',
  'metadata': {'file_directory': './KnowledgeFiles',
               'filename': 'faq.pdf',
               'filetype': 'application/pdf',
               'languages': ['eng'],
               'last_modified': '2026-10-10T22:36:54',
               'orig_elements': '',
               'page_number': 2},
  'text': 'must be fixed to the floor or wall. Movable items such as chairs or '
          'dining tables are not\n'
          '\n'
          'suitable for this purpose. For example, it is appropriate to '
          'securely tie the dog to a table that\n'
          '\n'
          'is firmly fixed to the floor, or to a hook securely installed on a '
          'wall.\n'
          '\n'
          'Q3: If a dog is already placed in a pet stroller or a pet carrier, '
          'is the customer still required\n'
          '\n'
          'to control the dog in the manner prescribed by law?',
  'type': 'CompositeElement'},
 {'element_id': '7d3cf27d-1b6c-42a7-8cdd-99eb29930e31',
  'metadata': {'file_directory': './KnowledgeFiles',
               'filename': 'faq.pdf',
               'filetype': 'application/pdf',
               'languages': ['eng'],
               'last_modified': '2026-10-10T22:36:54',
               'orig_elements': '',
               'page_number': 2},
  'text': 'A3: Even if the dog is inside a pet carrier or stroller, the '
          'customer must still comply with the\n'
          '\n'
          'legal requirement of having the dog securely held on a leash by an '
          'adult or tied to a fixture,\n'
          '\n'
          'in order to address potential dangerous situations that may arise '
          'should the dog be startled\n'
          '\n'
          'or agitated by external stimuli.\n'
          '\n'
          'Q4: What are "fighting dogs"?\n'
          '\n'
          'A4: Pursuant to the Dangerous Dogs Regulation (Cap. 167D), Pit Bull '
          'Terrier, Dogo Argentino,',
  'type': 'CompositeElement'},
 {'element_id': '198008c5-8b95-4f70-bad4-22784edde359',
  'metadata': {'file_directory': './KnowledgeFiles',
               'filename': 'faq.pdf',
               'filetype': 'application/pdf',
               'languages': ['eng'],
               'last_modified': '2026-10-10T22:36:54',
               'orig_elements': '',
               'page_number': 3},
  'text': 'Japanese Tosa, Fila Braziliero and their crossbreeds are classified '
          'as “fighting dogs”. Please\n'
          '\n'
          'refer to the photos below for your reference.\n'
          '\n'
          'As of the end of 2025, there were approximately 20 fighting dogs in '
          'Hong Kong.\n'
          '\n'
          'Q5: What are "known dangerous dogs"?\n'
          '\n'
          'A5: Under the Dangerous Dogs Regulation (Cap. 167D), a dog may be '
          'classified as a "known\n'
          '\n'
          'dangerous dog" if a magistrate determines it to be so under '
          'specific circumstances. This',
  'type': 'CompositeElement'},
 {'element_id': 'f1926c51-1006-4b97-874a-ffdc29fe7eae',
  'metadata': {'file_directory': './KnowledgeFiles',
               'filename': 'faq.pdf',
               'filetype': 'application/pdf',
               'languages': ['eng'],
               'last_modified': '2026-10-10T22:36:54',
               'orig_elements': '',
               'page_number': 3},
  'text': 'typically includes dogs that, without provocation, have attacked a '
          'person or a domestic\n'
          '\n'
          'animal, resulting in severe physical injury or death.\n'
          '\n'
          'As of the end of 2025, there were approximately 20 "known dangerous '
          'dogs" in Hong Kong.\n'
          '\n'
          'Q6: How can we distinguish between "fighting dogs" and "known '
          'dangerous dogs" as\n'
          '\n'
          'specified in the legislation?\n'
          '\n'
          "A6: Under the Dangerous Dogs Regulation (Cap. 167D), 'fighting "
          "dogs' and dogs declared as",
  'type': 'CompositeElement'},
 {'element_id': '73573b53-1fe3-42cd-b6d0-038024ca0b49',
  'metadata': {'file_directory': './KnowledgeFiles',
               'filename': 'faq.pdf',
               'filetype': 'application/pdf',
               'languages': ['eng'],
               'last_modified': '2026-10-10T22:36:54',
               'orig_elements': '',
               'page_number': 4},
  'text': "'known dangerous dogs' by a court must at all times wear a specific "
          'collar for identification\n'
          '\n'
          'purposes (see image below). In addition, such dogs must also wear a '
          'muzzle and be\n'
          '\n'
          'controlled with a leash not exceeding 1.5 metres in length. If in '
          'doubt about the situation,\n'
          '\n'
          'restaurant staff should request the customer with the dog to '
          'clearly state whether their dog\n'
          '\n'
          "is a 'fighting dog' or a 'known dangerous dog'.",
  'type': 'CompositeElement'},
 {'element_id': 'd4565834-4f4a-4ad3-85f8-4e698fdc7063',
  'metadata': {'file_directory': './KnowledgeFiles',
               'filename': 'faq.pdf',
               'filetype': 'application/pdf',
               'languages': ['eng'],
               'last_modified': '2026-10-10T22:36:54',
               'orig_elements': '',
               'page_number': 5},
  'text': 'Licencing condition\n'
          '\n'
          'Display of designated signage\n'
          '\n'
          'Q7: How and where should the restaurant operator display the '
          'designated signage after\n'
          '\n'
          'the restaurant is granted permission to allow dogs to enter?\n'
          '\n'
          'A7: Restaurants granted permission by the FEHD shall display at all '
          'times an A3 size signage\n'
          '\n'
          'designated by the department in a conspicuous place near the main '
          'entrances of the premises\n'
          '\n'
          'and must be clearly visible to customers before they enter the '
          'restaurant. Displaying the',
  'type': 'CompositeElement'},
 {'element_id': 'd4b73462-0edc-46ac-94f0-bac1c8f88219',
  'metadata': {'file_directory': './KnowledgeFiles',
               'filename': 'faq.pdf',
               'filetype': 'application/pdf',
               'languages': ['eng'],
               'last_modified': '2026-10-10T22:36:54',
               'orig_elements': '',
               'page_number': 5},
  'text': 'designated signage at the cashier counter, or allowing it to be '
          'obstructed or covered by other\n'
          '\n'
          'objects, will be regarded as a breach of the licensing conditions. '
          'Furthermore, restaurant\n'
          '\n'
          'operators must comply with any instructions given by FEHD officers '
          'regarding the manner\n'
          '\n'
          'of displaying the designated signage.\n'
          '\n'
          'Q8: When is the restaurant operator required to display or remove '
          'the relevant signage?',
  'type': 'CompositeElement'},
 {'element_id': '26c01af8-8f5f-46fe-a8bd-b9c4b885ca67',
  'metadata': {'file_directory': './KnowledgeFiles',
               'filename': 'faq.pdf',
               'filetype': 'application/pdf',
               'languages': ['eng'],
               'last_modified': '2026-10-10T22:36:54',
               'orig_elements': '',
               'page_number': 5},
  'text': 'A8: From the effective date of the permission to allow dogs to '
          'enter the restaurant, the permitted\n'
          '\n'
          'restaurant must display the designated signage at all times, in '
          'accordance with the licensing\n'
          '\n'
          'conditions. Should the restaurant voluntarily surrender the '
          'permission, or if the permission\n'
          '\n'
          'is cancelled due to a breach of regulations, the licensee must '
          'immediately remove the\n'
          '\n'
          'designated signage upon the cancellation of such permission.',
  'type': 'CompositeElement'},
 {'element_id': '6cc306b6-71c7-45e7-aa54-bfc35307df6b',
  'metadata': {'file_directory': './KnowledgeFiles',
               'filename': 'faq.pdf',
               'filetype': 'application/pdf',
               'languages': ['eng'],
               'last_modified': '2026-10-10T22:36:54',
               'orig_elements': '',
               'page_number': 6},
  'text': 'Q9: If a restaurant operator wishes to designate certain days or '
          'time slots during which\n'
          '\n'
          'dogs are not allowed to enter the restaurant, can they remove or '
          'put away the displayed\n'
          '\n'
          'signage displayed at the entrance?\n'
          '\n'
          'A9: Operators may decide to allow dogs to enter their premises only '
          'on certain days or during\n'
          '\n'
          'specific time slots. However, they must still display the '
          'designated signage in a conspicuous\n'
          '\n'
          'location at all main entrances at all times, in accordance with the '
          'licensing conditions. The',
  'type': 'CompositeElement'},
 {'element_id': '572f549e-4433-42bd-a62e-37dbd140c66b',
  'metadata': {'file_directory': './KnowledgeFiles',
               'filename': 'faq.pdf',
               'filetype': 'application/pdf',
               'languages': ['eng'],
               'last_modified': '2026-10-10T22:36:54',
               'orig_elements': '',
               'page_number': 6},
  'text': 'signage must not be removed at any time. Operators should display '
          'additional notices\n'
          '\n'
          'explaining the arrangements for different time slots or days, so as '
          'to facilitate customer\n'
          '\n'
          'understanding and avoid unnecessary misunderstandings.',
  'type': 'CompositeElement'},
 {'element_id': 'cf458a3c-966d-41ab-bfdc-94468e0db342',
  'metadata': {'file_directory': './KnowledgeFiles',
               'filename': 'faq.pdf',
               'filetype': 'application/pdf',
               'languages': ['eng'],
               'last_modified': '2026-10-10T22:36:54',
               'orig_elements': '',
               'page_number': 6},
  'text': 'Operational Management\n'
          '\n'
          'Q10: What should be noted if a restaurant has bar counter seating?\n'
          '\n'
          'A10: Bar counter seating is typically connected to the food counter '
          'or the area where food and\n'
          '\n'
          'drinks are prepared, and there is usually no permanent fixed '
          'partition reaching the ceiling\n'
          '\n'
          'separating the two.\n'
          '\n'
          'Allowing dogs to be present at such bar counter seating may '
          'increase food safety risks.\n'
          '\n'
          'Therefore, restaurant operators must prohibit customers with dogs '
          'from sitting at bar counter',
  'type': 'CompositeElement'},
 {'element_id': '9bf28340-da84-449a-8803-9b74fe37d6aa',
  'metadata': {'file_directory': './KnowledgeFiles',
               'filename': 'faq.pdf',
               'filetype': 'application/pdf',
               'languages': ['eng'],
               'last_modified': '2026-10-10T22:36:54',
               'orig_elements': '',
               'page_number': 6},
  'text': 'seating and should clearly communicate this arrangement to '
          'customers.\n'
          '\n'
          'Q11: What should be noted if a restaurant has a buffet counter / '
          'salad bar?\n'
          '\n'
          'A11: The buffet counter / salad bar is where food is displayed. '
          'Allowing dogs to be in close\n'
          '\n'
          'proximity may pose safety and food hygiene risks. Therefore, it '
          'must be ensured that dogs\n'
          '\n'
          'cannot reach the food. When assigning seats to customers with dogs, '
          'restaurant operators',
  'type': 'CompositeElement'},
 {'element_id': 'b3ea7e3a-7882-4ec3-95f2-d38803f4e964',
  'metadata': {'file_directory': './KnowledgeFiles',
               'filename': 'faq.pdf',
               'filetype': 'application/pdf',
               'languages': ['eng'],
               'last_modified': '2026-10-10T22:36:54',
               'orig_elements': '',
               'page_number': 7},
  'text': 'must ensure that dogs are not allowed within 1.5 metres of the '
          'buffet counter / salad bar.\n'
          '\n'
          'Q12: Under the licensing conditions, restaurants are prohibited '
          'from heating food at the\n'
          '\n'
          'table. However, if electric heating or small heating devices such '
          'as alcohol burners are\n'
          '\n'
          'used instead of traditional gas stoves, would such methods be '
          'exempt from this\n'
          '\n'
          'restriction? Are there any exceptions?\n'
          '\n'
          'A12: The prohibition on heating food at the table is intended to '
          'ensure the safety of customers,',
  'type': 'CompositeElement'},
 {'element_id': '5b1d72c1-98a1-4f58-831e-278266d9ac66',
  'metadata': {'file_directory': './KnowledgeFiles',
               'filename': 'faq.pdf',
               'filetype': 'application/pdf',
               'languages': ['eng'],
               'last_modified': '2026-10-10T22:36:54',
               'orig_elements': '',
               'page_number': 7},
  'text': 'staff, and animals. Therefore, both open-flame heating and electric '
          'heating are prohibited.\n'
          '\n'
          'Beverage warming devices used by some restaurants, such as small '
          'candles or electric\n'
          '\n'
          'coasters used in coffee shops and Chinese teahouses, are not '
          'subject to this restriction.\n'
          '\n'
          'Q13: If a restaurant has designated a portion of its premises as a '
          '"dog-friendly area," can\n'
          '\n'
          'food be heated at tables in the "non-dog-friendly area"?',
  'type': 'CompositeElement'},
 {'element_id': 'b5ff0d23-0dfd-4ad3-87c5-f4b8fb057d01',
  'metadata': {'file_directory': './KnowledgeFiles',
               'filename': 'faq.pdf',
               'filetype': 'application/pdf',
               'languages': ['eng'],
               'last_modified': '2026-10-10T22:36:54',
               'orig_elements': '',
               'page_number': 8},
  'text': 'A13: No. For safety reasons, the licensing conditions that allow '
          'dogs to enter the restaurant apply\n'
          '\n'
          'to the entire area of the approved premises. This is to minimise '
          'the risk of injury to restaurant\n'
          '\n'
          'staff, customers, and dogs in the event of accidents such as '
          'spilled hot food or overturned\n'
          '\n'
          'heating appliances during any unforeseen circumstances.',
  'type': 'CompositeElement'},
 {'element_id': '5c49674a-c0fd-4f71-9022-a6a98e6d2243',
  'metadata': {'file_directory': './KnowledgeFiles',
               'filename': 'faq.pdf',
               'filetype': 'application/pdf',
               'languages': ['eng'],
               'last_modified': '2026-10-10T22:36:54',
               'orig_elements': '',
               'page_number': 8},
  'text': 'Cancellation of permission\n'
          '\n'
          'Q14: Can a restaurant that has been granted permission to allow '
          'dogs to enter voluntarily\n'
          '\n'
          'cancel the permission?\n'
          '\n'
          'A14: Yes. A permitted restaurant may apply to the Department in '
          'writing. The Department will\n'
          '\n'
          'issue the permission for cancellation as early as four working days '
          'after receipt of the\n'
          '\n'
          'application. Once the permission is cancelled, the restaurant must '
          'immediately remove the\n'
          '\n'
          'designated signage displayed at the conspicuous location of the '
          'entrances.',
  'type': 'CompositeElement'},
 {'element_id': '05dfa83b-9871-4f25-8998-3c041e62cd69',
  'metadata': {'file_directory': './KnowledgeFiles',
               'filename': 'faq.pdf',
               'filetype': 'application/pdf',
               'languages': ['eng'],
               'last_modified': '2026-10-10T22:36:54',
               'orig_elements': '',
               'page_number': 8},
  'text': 'Q15: What are the penalties if an approved restaurant breaches the '
          'licensing conditions or\n'
          '\n'
          'dog-related legislation?\n'
          '\n'
          'A15: If a permitted restaurant is issued with three warning letters '
          'within a 12-month period for\n'
          '\n'
          'breaching one or more of the licensing conditions or statutory '
          'requirements governing the\n'
          '\n'
          'admission of dogs into restaurants, its permission for dogs to '
          'enter may be cancelled. The\n'
          '\n'
          'restaurant will not be accepted to re-apply for such permission for '
          'a period of one year.',
  'type': 'CompositeElement'},
 {'element_id': '4879dd51-07af-4259-a2fd-af1cdc4cc4b7',
  'metadata': {'file_directory': './KnowledgeFiles',
               'filename': 'faq.pdf',
               'filetype': 'application/pdf',
               'languages': ['eng'],
               'last_modified': '2026-10-10T22:36:54',
               'orig_elements': '',
               'page_number': 8},
  'text': 'Additionally, if a restaurant is prosecuted for contravening the '
          'Public Health and Municipal\n'
          '\n'
          'Services Ordinance (Cap. 132) or its subsidiary legislation '
          '(including legislation relating to\n'
          '\n'
          'the admission of dogs into restaurants) and accumulates sufficient '
          'demerit points due to\n'
          '\n'
          'convictions within a 12-month period, its food business license may '
          'be suspended or\n'
          '\n'
          'cancelled in accordance with the FEHD’s existing Demerit Points '
          'System.\n'
          '\n'
          'Serving food to dogs',
  'type': 'CompositeElement'},
 {'element_id': '2c0850a4-1533-4c0f-9ac2-4de24f9b9117',
  'metadata': {'file_directory': './KnowledgeFiles',
               'filename': 'faq.pdf',
               'filetype': 'application/pdf',
               'languages': ['eng'],
               'last_modified': '2026-10-10T22:36:54',
               'orig_elements': '',
               'page_number': 9},
  'text': 'Q16: Are restaurants permitted to provide food for dogs?\n'
          '\n'
          'A16: To ensure food safety and environmental hygiene, the licensing '
          'conditions stipulate that no\n'
          '\n'
          'cooking or preparation of dog food on the premises is allowed. This '
          'prohibition covers\n'
          '\n'
          'heating or reheating processes. Restaurants may provide or sell '
          'pre-packaged, ready-to-eat\n'
          '\n'
          'dog food that requires no further processing, such as dry kibble, '
          'vacuum-packed dog food,',
  'type': 'CompositeElement'},
 {'element_id': '930514c2-d90f-48de-94b6-a288587009b0',
  'metadata': {'file_directory': './KnowledgeFiles',
               'filename': 'faq.pdf',
               'filetype': 'application/pdf',
               'languages': ['eng'],
               'last_modified': '2026-10-10T22:36:54',
               'orig_elements': '',
               'page_number': 9},
  'text': 'and canned dog food. However, they must not heat or reheat such '
          'food, including by using\n'
          '\n'
          'hot water or a microwave oven.\n'
          '\n'
          'Q17: Are bread and cakes considered "pre-packaged dry dog food"?\n'
          '\n'
          'A17: Pre-packaged dry dog food generally refers to items such as '
          'dog biscuits, freeze-dried meat\n'
          '\n'
          'strips or pellets, and freeze-dried fruits or vegetables. It does '
          'not include bread or cakes.\n'
          '\n'
          'Q18: Can pre-packaged dry dog food, vacuum-packed pet food, or '
          'canned dog food be\n'
          '\n'
          'heated?',
  'type': 'CompositeElement'},
 {'element_id': 'd163e5dd-eeac-46fe-a95b-e3409837410c',
  'metadata': {'file_directory': './KnowledgeFiles',
               'filename': 'faq.pdf',
               'filetype': 'application/pdf',
               'languages': ['eng'],
               'last_modified': '2026-10-10T22:36:54',
               'orig_elements': '',
               'page_number': 9},
  'text': 'A18: No. If restaurant staff provide or sell processed dog food to '
          'customers, for instance, by\n'
          '\n'
          'removing the packaging and heating the food, it constitutes a '
          'breach of the licensing\n'
          '\n'
          'conditions.\n'
          '\n'
          'Q19: Are restaurants allowed to provide facilities within the '
          'seating area for customers to',
  'type': 'CompositeElement'},
 {'element_id': '1d3fb4c9-571b-4de7-a2da-d7200b4425bc',
  'metadata': {'file_directory': './KnowledgeFiles',
               'filename': 'faq.pdf',
               'filetype': 'application/pdf',
               'languages': ['eng'],
               'last_modified': '2026-10-10T22:36:54',
               'orig_elements': '',
               'page_number': 9},
  'text': 'heat dog food themselves?\n'
          '\n'
          'A19: The licensing conditions do not prohibit the provision of '
          'facilities on restaurant premises\n'
          '\n'
          'for customers to heat dog food themselves. If such facilities are '
          'provided, clear usage\n'
          '\n'
          'guidelines should be set out to ensure safety and environmental '
          'hygiene.\n'
          '\n'
          "Q20: Can restaurants sell items related to facilitating dogs' entry "
          'into the premises, such as',
  'type': 'CompositeElement'},
 {'element_id': '3cbcc802-895e-4980-93b8-9e17a8ee8969',
  'metadata': {'file_directory': './KnowledgeFiles',
               'filename': 'faq.pdf',
               'filetype': 'application/pdf',
               'languages': ['eng'],
               'last_modified': '2026-10-10T22:36:54',
               'orig_elements': '',
               'page_number': 10},
  'text': 'pee pads, leashes, muzzles, etc.?\n'
          '\n'
          'A20: Under normal circumstances, as long as food safety and '
          'environmental hygiene are not\n'
          '\n'
          'affected, the FEHD does not prohibit restaurants from selling small '
          'merchandise. Permitted\n'
          '\n'
          'restaurants may sell pee pads, leashes, muzzles, and similar items.',
  'type': 'CompositeElement'},
 {'element_id': '201bd1c3-d46e-41c9-9338-1183eb0467d3',
  'metadata': {'file_directory': './KnowledgeFiles',
               'filename': 'faq.pdf',
               'filetype': 'application/pdf',
               'languages': ['eng'],
               'last_modified': '2026-10-10T22:36:54',
               'orig_elements': '',
               'page_number': 10},
  'text': 'Management and Control of Dogs\n'
          '\n'
          'Q21: Dogs are not allowed to be on dining tables, but can they be '
          'held or seated on dining\n'
          '\n'
          'chairs and still come into contact with the table?\n'
          '\n'
          'A21: According to the licensing conditions, no dog shall be allowed '
          'on any dining table. This\n'
          '\n'
          'licensing condition is based on safety considerations and aims to '
          'protect the safety of\n'
          '\n'
          'restaurant staff, customers, and dogs, preventing accidents in '
          'which a dog, suddenly startled',
  'type': 'CompositeElement'},
 {'element_id': 'e906319e-fb87-49ff-aab2-2bfa6f8704dd',
  'metadata': {'file_directory': './KnowledgeFiles',
               'filename': 'faq.pdf',
               'filetype': 'application/pdf',
               'languages': ['eng'],
               'last_modified': '2026-10-10T22:36:54',
               'orig_elements': '',
               'page_number': 10},
  'text': 'or excited, could knock over tabletop appliances, hot soup, or hot '
          'oil.\n'
          '\n'
          'As to whether dogs are allowed to be on dining chairs, given that '
          'individual restaurants may\n'
          '\n'
          'have different premises, environments, and operations, restaurant '
          'operators may refer to the\n'
          '\n'
          'key factors set out in the coming "Guideline on Good Practices and '
          'Behaviour" and make\n'
          '\n'
          'their own arrangements based on actual circumstances.\n'
          '\n'
          'It must be noted that regardless of whether a dog is held or seated '
          'on a dining chair, it must',
  'type': 'CompositeElement'},
 {'element_id': '96a5dcf9-c091-470a-87ed-9c3d46d5ee32',
  'metadata': {'file_directory': './KnowledgeFiles',
               'filename': 'faq.pdf',
               'filetype': 'application/pdf',
               'languages': ['eng'],
               'last_modified': '2026-10-10T22:36:54',
               'orig_elements': '',
               'page_number': 10},
  'text': 'not come into contact with the dining table top, and dog food must '
          'not be placed on the\n'
          '\n'
          'dining table for the dog to consume.\n'
          '\n'
          'Q22: Dogs are not allowed to use "reusable utensils" What utensils '
          'can dogs use to eat in',
  'type': 'CompositeElement'},
 {'element_id': '7ab457b1-f842-43f2-92ff-40bf9bd9b585',
  'metadata': {'file_directory': './KnowledgeFiles',
               'filename': 'faq.pdf',
               'filetype': 'application/pdf',
               'languages': ['eng'],
               'last_modified': '2026-10-10T22:36:54',
               'orig_elements': '',
               'page_number': 11},
  'text': 'a restaurant?\n'
          '\n'
          'A22: To protect public health and ensure that humans and dogs do '
          'not share tableware, the\n'
          '\n'
          'licensing conditions stipulated that reusable utensils shall not be '
          'provided to dogs on the\n'
          '\n'
          'premises that are intended for human use. Restaurants may provide '
          'or sell single-use non-\n'
          '\n'
          'plastic utensils or crockery for dogs to use. Dog owners may also '
          'bring their own tableware',
  'type': 'CompositeElement'},
 {'element_id': '16ed96a3-46bb-4e82-8a20-726499d0ab78',
  'metadata': {'file_directory': './KnowledgeFiles',
               'filename': 'faq.pdf',
               'filetype': 'application/pdf',
               'languages': ['eng'],
               'last_modified': '2026-10-10T22:36:54',
               'orig_elements': '',
               'page_number': 11},
  'text': 'for their dogs to use.\n'
          '\n'
          'Q23: If a dog defecates or urinates inside a restaurant, who is '
          'responsible for cleaning it\n'
          '\n'
          'up? Can the restaurant charge a cleaning fee for this?\n'
          '\n'
          'A23: At present, the Food Business Regulation and licensing '
          'conditions require that restaurants\n'
          '\n'
          'maintain cleanliness and hygiene at all times to ensure food safety '
          'and environmental\n'
          '\n'
          'hygiene. This is a fundamental responsibility of restaurant '
          'operators. On this premise,',
  'type': 'CompositeElement'},
 {'element_id': 'a1020d72-5938-4b94-999f-1dc8a80fbd6b',
  'metadata': {'file_directory': './KnowledgeFiles',
               'filename': 'faq.pdf',
               'filetype': 'application/pdf',
               'languages': ['eng'],
               'last_modified': '2026-10-10T22:36:54',
               'orig_elements': '',
               'page_number': 11},
  'text': 'restaurant operators may formulate arrangements for cleaning up dog '
          'waste based on their\n'
          '\n'
          'own circumstances. For example, if a restaurant intends to charge a '
          'cleaning fee to\n'
          '\n'
          'customers who soil the premises, the operator must clearly inform '
          'customers of this in\n'
          '\n'
          'advance to avoid disputes. Even if the customer does not clean up '
          'the dog waste\n'
          '\n'
          'themselves, the restaurant must clean it up immediately; failure to '
          'do so constitutes a',
  'type': 'CompositeElement'},
 {'element_id': 'ed715816-5170-46f4-9e49-514b62d6c39a',
  'metadata': {'file_directory': './KnowledgeFiles',
               'filename': 'faq.pdf',
               'filetype': 'application/pdf',
               'languages': ['eng'],
               'last_modified': '2026-10-10T22:36:54',
               'orig_elements': '',
               'page_number': 11},
  'text': 'breach of the licensing conditions. Depending on the circumstances, '
          'the restaurant may\n'
          '\n'
          'also be in contravention of food business regulations for failing '
          'to keep the premises clean.\n'
          '\n'
          'When making these arrangements, restaurant operators should also '
          'refer to the coming\n'
          '\n'
          '"Guideline on Good Practices and Behaviour" issued by the FEHD, '
          'which sets out factors\n'
          '\n'
          'to consider, such as providing designated rubbish bins for '
          'customers or staff to dispose of',
  'type': 'CompositeElement'},
 {'element_id': '83ce0bae-3e90-43a3-a02e-93059572e12a',
  'metadata': {'file_directory': './KnowledgeFiles',
               'filename': 'faq.pdf',
               'filetype': 'application/pdf',
               'languages': ['eng'],
               'last_modified': '2026-10-10T22:36:54',
               'orig_elements': '',
               'page_number': 11},
  'text': 'dog waste. It should be noted, however, that such rubbish bins must '
          'not be placed inside\n'
          '\n'
          'food rooms.',
  'type': 'CompositeElement'},
 {'element_id': 'cd8a07aa-c592-4ce5-8473-20288ad392b0',
  'metadata': {'file_directory': './KnowledgeFiles',
               'filename': 'faq.pdf',
               'filetype': 'application/pdf',
               'languages': ['eng'],
               'last_modified': '2026-10-10T22:36:54',
               'orig_elements': '',
               'page_number': 12},
  'text': 'Incident Handling\n'
          '\n'
          'Q24: In the event of an incident where a dog bites a person or '
          'another animal, who will be\n'
          '\n'
          'liable? Is the restaurant required to report it to the FEHD?\n'
          '\n'
          'A24: Dog owners bear the responsibility to restrict and control '
          'their dogs. Under the Rabies\n'
          '\n'
          'Ordinance (Cap. 421), if a dog is found in any public place '
          '(including restaurants) without\n'
          '\n'
          'being on a leash or otherwise under control and bites a person, the '
          'keeper of the dog is',
  'type': 'CompositeElement'},
 {'element_id': '64a89e3d-7641-43e3-8c7b-06b920009321',
  'metadata': {'file_directory': './KnowledgeFiles',
               'filename': 'faq.pdf',
               'filetype': 'application/pdf',
               'languages': ['eng'],
               'last_modified': '2026-10-10T22:36:54',
               'orig_elements': '',
               'page_number': 12},
  'text': 'guilty of an offense and liable to a level 3 fine, unless they can '
          'prove that all reasonable\n'
          '\n'
          'measures were taken to prevent the biting or that the dog was '
          'intentionally provoked.\n'
          '\n'
          'Furthermore, the keeper must notify the nearest police station '
          'without delay and detain the\n'
          '\n'
          'dog in a secure manner, isolated from other animals, for a period '
          'specified by the police;\n'
          '\n'
          'failure to do so is an offence liable to a level 3 fine.',
  'type': 'CompositeElement'},
 {'element_id': '0ea9b225-0685-4897-a451-9f3bcd19d897',
  'metadata': {'file_directory': './KnowledgeFiles',
               'filename': 'faq.pdf',
               'filetype': 'application/pdf',
               'languages': ['eng'],
               'last_modified': '2026-10-10T22:36:54',
               'orig_elements': '',
               'page_number': 12},
  'text': 'The FEHD has stipulated in its licensing conditions that if a dog '
          'causes injury to any\n'
          '\n'
          'person on the premises and the matter is reported to the police, '
          'the licensee must report\n'
          '\n'
          'the case to the FEHD using the designated form within two working '
          'days of the occurrence.\n'
          '\n'
          'Restaurant operators may also refer to the coming "Guideline on '
          'Good Practices and\n'
          '\n'
          'Behaviour" to formulate response plans, which include measures such '
          'as consoling',
  'type': 'CompositeElement'},
 {'element_id': 'ab32b9f1-6c37-4470-bb96-04b9dd0f934f',
  'metadata': {'file_directory': './KnowledgeFiles',
               'filename': 'faq.pdf',
               'filetype': 'application/pdf',
               'languages': ['eng'],
               'last_modified': '2026-10-10T22:36:54',
               'orig_elements': '',
               'page_number': 12},
  'text': 'affected customers and reminding dog owners of their legal '
          'responsibilities.',
  'type': 'CompositeElement'}]
