               'languages': ['eng'],
               'last_modified': '2026-10-10T22:35:06',
               'orig_elements': '',
               'page_number': 2},
  'text': 'entrance at all times.\n'
          '\n'
          '1.7\n'
          '\n'
          'Restaurant operators may, according to their actual circumstances, '
          'decide whether to\n'
          '\n'
          'designate dog-friendly zones. If they decide to do so, the '
          'provision of physical barriers\n'
          '\n'
          '(e.g. gates or hoardings) is advisable to prevent dogs from '
          'entering other areas. If\n'
          '\n'
          'permission for an outside seating accommodation (OSA) has already '
          'been granted,\n'
          '\n'
          'priority may be accorded to designating the OSA, which is more '
