               'languages': ['eng'],
               'last_modified': '2026-10-10T22:35:06',
               'orig_elements': '',
               'page_number': 9},
  'text': 'Response to incidents\n'
          '\n'
          '1.38\n'
          '\n'
          'In the event that a dog barks persistently, stares at people, '
          'exhibits aggressive behaviour,\n'
          '\n'
          'or causes nuisance to other diners, restaurant operators should, '
          'when it is safe to do so,\n'
          '\n'
          'ask the customer with the dog to take appropriate control measures, '
          'including\n'
          '\n'
          'temporarily removing the dog from the premises. The provision of '
          'takeaway\n'
          '\n'
          'packaging services may be considered to assist diners who need to '
          'leave early in taking',
  'type': 'CompositeElement'},
 {'element_id': 'f8e95036-fed8-474f-9a44-58aac5ab0c4f',
  'metadata': {'file_directory': './KnowledgeFiles',
               'filename': 'Guidelines on Good Practices and Behaviour for '
                           'Dog-Friendly Restaurants (Restaurant '
                           'Operators).pdf',
               'filetype': 'application/pdf',
               'languages': ['eng'],
               'last_modified': '2026-10-10T22:35:06',
               'orig_elements': '',
               'page_number': 9},
  'text': 'their unfinished meals away.\n'
          '\n'
          '1.39\n'
          '\n'
          'If a customer without dogs feels uneasy or is unable to continue '
          'dining due to a dog’s\n'
          '\n'
          'behaviour (including but not limited to noise, hygiene issues, or '
          'safety concerns), a\n'
          '\n'
          'reasonable solution should be provided by the food premises as far '
          'as possible, such as\n'
          '\n'
          'assisting with a seat change or offering takeaway packaging '
          'services so that the\n'
          '\n'
          'customer can take the unfinished meal away.',
  'type': 'CompositeElement'},
 {'element_id': '16551a01-4188-436c-800d-f35dfafbb1ed',
  'metadata': {'file_directory': './KnowledgeFiles',
               'filename': 'Guidelines on Good Practices and Behaviour for '
                           'Dog-Friendly Restaurants (Restaurant '
                           'Operators).pdf',
               'filetype': 'application/pdf',
               'languages': ['eng'],
               'last_modified': '2026-10-10T22:35:06',
               'orig_elements': '',
               'page_number': 9},
  'text': '1.40 The Rabies Ordinance (Cap. 421) sets out the arrangements for '
          'handling bites by\n'
          '\n'
          'animals (including dogs). The restaurant operator should remind the '
          'customer with\n'
          '\n'
          'the dog concerned to report the incident to the Police. If '
          'necessary, the restaurant\n'
          '\n'
          'operator may also proactively contact the Police and should '
          'promptly notify its\n'
          '\n'
          'insurance company to handle the related legal and claims matters. '
          'With the consent of',
  'type': 'CompositeElement'},
 {'element_id': '6966fbd5-be79-446a-a8d8-844a20910fab',
  'metadata': {'file_directory': './KnowledgeFiles',
               'filename': 'Guidelines on Good Practices and Behaviour for '
